# swarm.config — the ONE source of truth for which Claude model every factory
# claude launch runs on (#448, learning L6): the swarm worker (.sandcastle/
# main.mts), the healer (.sandcastle/heal.sh), the rehearsal reporter/healer
# (rehearsal-report.sh), the session runner, triage, and the landing rebase
# rescue (all via model-lib.sh). Plain KEY=value so the SAME bytes are BOTH
# sourceable by bash (model-lib.sh) and parseable by node (main.mts) — the
# consumers can no longer drift to different hardcoded models the way
# main.mts and heal.sh silently could, nor silently inherit whatever default
# model the host user's claude CLI happens to resolve.
#
# Changing SWARM_MODEL here is the one-line commit that moves the whole fleet.
#
# SWARM_MODEL_MAP maps each `model-<name>` tracker label (issue #448, additive
# like `priority`) to the model id a ticket carrying that label launches on. Its
# values are the ONLY models a ticket may select — the fail-fast allowlist that
# swarm_resolve_model (model-lib.sh) enforces: an unknown selector fails LOUD
# before any worker spawns, never a silent fall back to the default. Model ids
# are Anthropic aliases, editable here without touching any consumer.
SWARM_MODEL=claude-opus-4-8
SWARM_MODEL_MAP="opus=claude-opus-4-8 sonnet=claude-sonnet-4-5 haiku=claude-haiku-4-5"

# The diagnosis/repair tier, decoupled from the fleet's ticket-work model:
# SWARM_HEAL_MODEL runs the two healers (heal.sh and rehearsal-report.sh's
# tool-enabled heal leg); SWARM_REPORT_MODEL runs rehearsal-report.sh's
# headless red-leg diagnosis. Both read what a run left behind and judge it —
# work where diagnosis quality beats cost, so they may sit a tier above
# SWARM_MODEL. Every other claude launch (session runner, triage, landing
# rebase rescue) rides SWARM_MODEL itself.
SWARM_HEAL_MODEL=claude-opus-5
SWARM_REPORT_MODEL=claude-opus-5
